"W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -32.0, "lead_after": -32.0, "points_lost": 0.0, "best": "E7"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Cutting Points Cost a Whole Corner", "summary": "The 20k as White won by 32 points. GPT-6.1 Sol was level or close through the middle game, with Black's lead sitting at +5.3 after move 14, then slipped into a run of costly moves around the center cut and the bottom edge. By move 27 Black's lead stood at -25.6, and the rest of the game was White's to keep.", "moments": [{"turn": 17, "text": "D4 lost 5.7 points and turned Black's +1.4 into -4.3. The engine wanted F6, which would have kept the fight in the center. This was the first big swing against GPT-6.1 Sol."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "F4 lost 7.3 points, taking Black's lead from +0.1 to -7.2. The engine preferred B7. Black's long wall along row 4 was solid but did not stop White from building the left side."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "D2 lost 7.8 points and dropped Black from -9.4 to -17.2. On the board Black's stones on row 4 and row 3 were already strong, so this reach into the bottom, next to the lone white stone at E2, gave away the points the engine wanted spent at G5."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "The 20k's C6 lost 7.4 points, the one real blunder on White's side, yet Black's lead only moved from -23.5 to -16.1. At this point the game was far enough gone that even a White slip left Black well behind."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "E1 was the worst move of the game at 9.5 points, taking Black from -16.1 to -25.6. The engine's choice was H4, the open right side. Black kept filling in the bottom edge while White's wall stayed unchallenged."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script either read files/board, ran the `inspect` function on the current board plus one manually named move (chains, liberties, captures, empty regions), replayed the recorded game to verify it and build the SGF, or wrote notes. None looped over candidate moves, ranked them, or searched ahead, so the player chose all moves itself.", "stop": false}}